$ lib/verify/probe-spec.mjs --help
probe-spec — check an MP4 against the peak-media delivery spec

Usage: probe-spec [options] <file.mp4>

Checks H.264 High, yuv420p, AAC 48 kHz and faststart, plus any size/fps/duration given. Exit 0 if every check passes, 1 if any fails.

Options:
      --width             Expected video width
      --height            Expected video height
      --size <WxH>        Expected size, e.g. 1280x720 (same as --width/--height)
      --fps               Expected frame rate
      --duration-ms       Expected duration
      --tolerance-frames  Duration tolerance in frames (default: 1)
      --no-audio          Skip the audio checks (picture-only files such as plate renders)
      --json              Print the result as JSON
  -h, --help              Show this help and exit
      --version           Print the plugin version and exit

Examples:
  probe-spec out/final.mp4 --size 1280x720 --duration-ms 3000
exit=0
